  "commit": {
    "commit": {
      "date": "2026-11-20T13:52:28Z",
      "message": "ci(ios): stop the UI smoke spending its time limit waiting on tappable buttons (#4283)\n\n* ci(ios): stop the UI smoke spending its time limit waiting on tappable buttons\n\ntapReady() (#4249) always ran an XCTNSPredicateExpectation for isHittable, which\ncosts a fresh accessibility query plus a polling interval (about 3-5 s per tap on\nthe CI simulator, e.g. consent.no t=28.7s -> 31.5s) even when the element is\nalready hittable. With ~500 taps that moved the step from 37 to 46-50 min.\n\nTap immediately when the element exists and is hittable; keep the existing\nexists + hittable waits as the fallback so the flakiness protection is intact.\nRaise the step cap 50 -> 60 min (job limit is 120) for runner variance.\n\n* docs(changelog): note the iOS UI smoke speed-up"
    },
    "sha": "17a70e1368d8b823a670fed822a2ece6894e5bc5"
  },
